### 
2.1 Reward functions and learning processes



###### 
Definition 0 (Reward function).



A *reward function* R𝑅Ritalic\_R is a map from complete histories to real numbers777
These are sometimes called return functions, the discounted sum of rewards.
The results of this paper apply to traditional reward functions – that take values on all histories, not just complete histories – but they are easier to see in terms of return function..
Let ℛ={R:ℋn→ℝ}ℛconditional-set𝑅→subscriptℋ𝑛ℝ{\mathcal{R}}=\{R:{\mathcal{H}}\_{n}\to\mathbb{R}\}caligraphic\_R = { italic\_R : caligraphic\_H start\_POSTSUBSCRIPT italic\_n end\_POSTSUBSCRIPT → blackboard\_R } be the set of all reward functions.






