4 Properties of unriggable and riggable learning processes
-----------------------------------------------------------



If the learning process is influenceable, problems can emerge as this section will show.
Unriggable-but-influenceable processes allow the agent to choose “spurious” learning paths, even reversing standard learning, while a riggable learning process means the agent is willing to sacrifice value for all possible reward functions, with certainty, in order to push the ‘learnt’ outcome101010
Since the agent’s actions push the expected learning in one direction, this is not ‘learning’ in the commonly understood sense.
 in one direction or another.




